  "id": "self-protection",
  "term": "self-protection",
  "definition": "In this context, self-protection means a student’s awareness of risks to their voice and their use of preventive habits to avoid strain, fatigue, hoarseness, and misuse. It involves noticing vocal condition, regulating practice and rest, managing emotional readiness, and making sustainable choices during learning and performance preparation.",
